    {
      "id": "sol.hmmt-nov-guts-2013-p6.hmmt",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "\\(\\quad 5+3 \\sqrt{5}\\) If \\(x, y\\) denote the legs, then \\(x y=10\\) and \\(x^{2}+y^{2}=25\\), so \\(x+y+\\sqrt{x^{2}+y^{2}}=\\) \\(\\sqrt{\\left(x^{2}+y^{2}\\right)+2 x y}+5=\\sqrt{45}+5=5+3 \\sqrt{5}\\).",
